English translation (for reference only)

1. Definitions
   "The Software" means all content in this repository created by the rights holder,
   including code, templates, styles, the motion library, scripts, documentation,
   sample scripts, evaluation cases and demo images. Third-party materials are not
   part of the Software (see section 6).
   "Personal non-commercial use" means use by an individual for personal learning,
   research, hobby or non-profit personal creation, where neither the Software nor
   anything made with it earns any direct or indirect financial benefit.
   "Commercial use" means any other use, including: use by or for companies,
   organizations, studios, teams, employees, contractors or client projects; paid
   services, commercial content, marketing, advertising, branding, sales or promotion;
   videos or visuals made with the Software that earn income through ads, platform
   revenue sharing, paid content, sponsorships or brand deals; and integrating the
   Software into products, services, workflows or other software, or offering services
   based on it. Internal use, trials, not yet being profitable, or not charging clients
   separately does not make a use personal and non-commercial.

2. Personal non-commercial license
   Subject to this license, you get a free, worldwide, non-exclusive, non-transferable,
   non-sublicensable license, for personal non-commercial use only, to: use, copy and
   modify the Software; make videos and visuals for your own personal non-commercial
   content; and share the Software, modified or not, non-commercially, provided you keep
   this license and the copyright notice intact, mark modified files, charge nothing,
   and do not sublicense it under other terms.

3. Commercial use
   Any commercial use requires prior written commercial authorization from the rights
   holder and payment of the applicable license fee. See COMMERCIAL.md; contact:
   <联系邮箱>.

4. Reserved rights
   All rights not expressly granted are reserved. The rights holder may license the
   Software under other terms.

5. Termination
   Your rights terminate automatically if you breach this license. You must then stop
   using the Software and delete all copies you hold.

6. Third-party materials
   Third-party materials shipped with the Software (including the GSAP animation engine
   and the bundled fonts) are not relicensed by this license and remain under their own
   terms; see THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md.

7. Disclaimer
   THE SOFTWARE IS PROVIDED "AS IS", WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY KIND, EXPRESS OR IMPLIED,
   INCLUDING BUT NOT LIMITED TO THE WARRANTIES OF MERCHANTABILITY, FITNESS FOR A
   PARTICULAR PURPOSE AND NONINFRINGEMENT. IN NO EVENT SHALL THE RIGHTS HOLDER BE LIABLE
   FOR ANY CLAIM, DAMAGES OR OTHER LIABILITY ARISING FROM THE SOFTWARE OR ITS USE.
